<v Maya>actually doing in the American workforce right now.</v>

9
00:00:53.814 --> 00:01:04.740
<v Daniel>Which, I mean, is an incredibly necessary pivot because the gap between the marketing out of those tech companies and the actual reality on the ground. Well, that's where all the actual economic friction is happening.</v>

10
00:01:05.029 --> 00:01:05.809
<v Maya>Right. The real world.</v>

11
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:19.355
<v Daniel>Exactly. So to understand this, we first need to look at the baseline. Back in late 2024, economists Alexander Bick, Adam Blandin, and David Deming released this paper called Rapid Adoption of Generative AI.</v>

12
00:01:19.657 --> 00:01:21.158
<v Maya>Okay. Setting the stage.</v>

13
00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:32.009
<v Daniel>Right. And they found that workplace adoption of Gen AI was moving as fast as the early personal computer. But 27% of workers were using it for work in the prior week.</v>

14
