00:09:06.496 --> 00:09:07.957
<v Maya>all very screen-heavy stuff.</v>

93
00:09:08.257 --> 00:09:15.762
<v Daniel>Yeah. The bottom tasks explicitly involve interacting with patients, operating equipment, driving, or landscaping.</v>

94
00:09:16.082 --> 00:09:16.843
<v Maya>That makes total sense.</v>

95
00:09:17.663 --> 00:09:26.509
<v Daniel>Notably, any task where strict liability, physical danger, or the need for human care limits the use of an algorithm, well, it just sits at the very bottom of the adoption curve.</v>

96
00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:31.472
<v Maya>OK, but looking at this data, I'm highly skeptical of those task level limits.</v>

